    <string name="privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_analytics">Usage analytics is on by default, and the app tells you on first launch. The maintainer’s Umami service receives a random installation ID, app and device details, information about feature and permission use, and the results and duration of lyrics and translation operations. It does not receive song titles, lyrics, playback history, notification text, unique device identifiers, or API keys. The service may estimate region and sessions from IP addresses and request times. https://umi.luoh.org\n\nIf the app crashes, it temporarily stores a diagnostic record on your device containing the time, app version, exception type, and code location. The app sends the record the next time it starts and removes any record older than seven days.\n\nTo turn off analytics, go to Settings → About → Help improve the app. This stops reporting, deletes pending records, and resets the installation ID. Previously received records remain on the server. Updates keep your setting, and a fresh installation restores the default.</string>
    <string name="privacy_lyrics">When finding lyrics and album art, the app sends the song title, artist, album, and duration to LRCLIB, QQ Music, NetEase Cloud Music, or KuGou Music. It may also query the Apple iTunes Search API for localized song information. Settings automatically checks GitHub for updates at most once a day. Online services may record your IP address and request times.\n\nCustom LRC files stay on your device. Deleting them restores automatic matching. Uninstalling the app removes local settings and cached data.</string>
    <string name="privacy_permissions">Notification access reads the song information, album art, and playback progress shared by your music player. The app reads media volume through Android and sends playback commands only when you use its controls.\n\nDisplay over other apps lets the app show lyrics. A foreground service keeps the overlay running, and notification permission lets you lock, unlock, or close it from the notification panel.</string>
    <string name="privacy_summary">The app mainly processes data on your device. It has no accounts, advertising SDKs, or location features.</string>
    <string name="privacy_translation">Supplemental translation is off by default. With Google ML Kit, lyrics and translations stay on your device. ML Kit connects to the internet to download or update language packs and check compatibility, and it may report performance and usage metrics. https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/terms\n\nWith API translation, the app sends lyrics to the HTTPS service you configure. Data handling and charges depend on that service. Android Keystore encrypts the API key, and the key is excluded from system backups. You can clear downloaded language packs and cached translations separately.</string>
